The backend_test ATF cases use socketpair-backed DNS-SD mocks. They do not
need a running daemon or change the host resolver configuration.

The optional ipc_test helper exercises real libc NSS module loading and the
installed libdns_sd client against a private IPC server. Run it as root,
passing the absolute path to the built nss_dnssd.so.1. For example, from the
source root after building lib/libnss_dnssd:

    dnssd_objdir=$(bmake -C lib/libnss_dnssd -V .OBJDIR)
    env -i PATH=/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin LC_ALL=C \
        "$dnssd_objdir/tests/ipc_test" "$dnssd_objdir/nss_dnssd.so.1"

It creates a temporary chroot with private resolver configuration and copies
of the runtime libraries. A temporary UDP responder on 127.0.0.1:53 supplies
controlled fallback answers. It sends no external DNS queries and does not
start mdnsd or alter the live resolver configuration. It tests positive and
negative IPC replies, malformed-reply fallback, unavailable-daemon fallback,
and files-source precedence. The helper skips if it cannot use the private
loopback DNS address because that port is already occupied.

These tests do not validate the real daemon's upstream selection, cache TTL
expiry, negative caching, or configuration reload behavior.
